<node id="d29e9dfd-1897-408a-a17c-e48663ab1d13">
  <data key="d0">{"name":"Policy Modification Terms","text":"0 days written notice.\n\n7.2 Adding riders may require evidence of insurability.\n\n7.3 Beneficiary changes may be made at any time by written request.\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n\nIssued in Denver, Colorado\n\n[SIGNATURE]\n________________________\nPresident and CEO\nProtectPlus Family Insurance Co.\n\nDate: July 12, 2024\n\n═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════\n","summary":"This document specifies critical conditions governing an insurance policy, such as zero-day notice required for cancellation, the need for proof of insurability when adding riders, and the ability to change beneficiaries at any time through a written request. Issued by ProtectPlus Family Insurance Co. in Denver, Colorado, on July 12, 2024, it reflects standard contractual flexibilities and administrative procedures. The signature of the President and CEO confirms its formal issuance.","topics":["Insurance Policy Terms","Beneficiary Changes","Rider Additions","Policy Cancellation"],"facts":[{"name":"Zero-day notice requirement","sentence":"A policy requires zero days' written notice.","macro_topics":[],"chunk_topics":["written notice","policy terms","notice period"],"entities":[{"name":"0 days written notice","type":"CONCEPT","role":"immediate cancellation requirement","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Adding riders","type":"CONCEPT","role":"policy enhancement requiring proof","relational_anchors":["evidence of insurability"]},{"name":"Beneficiary changes","type":"CONCEPT","role":"modifiable via written request","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"Denver, Colorado","type":"LOCATION","role":"issuance location of policy","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"ProtectPlus Family Insurance Co.","type":"ORGANIZATION","role":"insurer issuing policy documents","relational_anchors":[]},{"name":"President and CEO","type":"PERSON","role":"executive signatory authority","relati