  <data key="d3">The designation of the Bennett Family Irrevocable Trust as a contingent beneficiary ensures coverage continuity in case primary beneficiaries like Christopher Bennett Jr. cannot inherit, though it does not alter his predetermined 20% entitlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">supplements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eb966bac-9408-45d8-8f12-961e2781e108" target="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74">
  <data key="d3">The contingent beneficiary designation specifies an alternative recipient for the death benefit when primary beneficiaries cannot claim it, providing necessary context for interpreting the payout conditions described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eb966bac-9408-45d8-8f12-961e2781e108" target="e225c316-9494-4db7-a2fa-eeff59066bd6">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the Bennett Family Irrevocable Trust as a contingent beneficiary is subject to modification due to the policy’s provision allowing beneficiary changes at any time through written request.</data>
