<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="6f640b89-f337-49ac-8e73-3d7620e5a591">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the insured die during the policy term with all premiums paid enables the disbursement of benefits to primary beneficiaries like Christopher Bennett Jr., making the eligibility condition foundational to the distribution process.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="5f65dda2-13f5-45fa-98d0-27d7030b8212">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the insured die while the policy is active and premiums are current enables Olivia Grace Bennett, as a named primary beneficiary, to receive her portion of the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="49f7760e-ed64-4d66-89e7-40dd8a8a3315">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the insured died during the policy term with full premium payments enables the disbursement of benefits, including Rachel Marie Bennett’s 60% portion.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="d43f31e6-1eed-48b5-aef6-74a3b52ebdc1">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable only if the insured dies while the policy is active and premiums are current, ensuring that Christopher Bennett Jr.’s 20% share is eligible for disbursement under those qualifying circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="1e05c4c2-d6ce-4d80-b83c-1a94c95e7fab">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is payable upon the insured’s death during the policy term and after all premiums are paid; this triggers the disbursement of funds, including Olivia Grace Bennett’s 20% share.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="eb966bac-9408-45d8-8f12-961e2781e108">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the insured die while the policy is active and premiums are current establishes the core trigger for the death benefit, making the role of the contingent beneficiary more meaningful in cases where primary beneficiaries are ineligible.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies while the policy is active and premiums are up to date, the insurer commits to paying the death benefit. This obligation is fulfilled by making the payment within 30 days of receiving acceptable proof of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74" target="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit is generally payable when the insured dies during the policy term with all premiums paid; however, this does not apply if death occurs due to suicide within two years, in which case only the total premiums paid are returned.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
