<edge source="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17" target="498d9179-3206-4b4a-ad0e-8d21b73e3d63">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid within 30 days of proof of death depends on the presence of identified beneficiaries such as Rachel Marie Bennett, whose designation makes the claim process applicable.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17" target="6f640b89-f337-49ac-8e73-3d7620e5a591">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid within 30 days of proof of death ensures timely fulfillment of obligations to all eligible beneficiaries, including Christopher Bennett Jr., whose designation makes him entitled to a share.</data>
  <data key="d4">timing condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17" target="5f65dda2-13f5-45fa-98d0-27d7030b8212">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the death benefit be paid within 30 days of receiving proof of death ensures timely fulfillment of obligations toward all named beneficiaries, including Olivia Grace Bennett.</data>
  <data key="d4">eligibility → timing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17" target="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to issue the death benefit within 30 days of receiving proof of death depends on the prior condition that the insured died during the policy term and all premiums were paid, ensuring the claim is eligible.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17" target="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc">
  <data key="d3">The 30-day payment timeline assumes no qualifying exceptions; however, if suicide occurs within two years, the insurer’s obligation shifts from paying the full death benefit to returning only premiums paid, thereby altering the applicability of the standard payment schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
