<edge source="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc" target="498d9179-3206-4b4a-ad0e-8d21b73e3d63">
  <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion clause modifies the distribution terms for beneficiaries like Rachel Marie Bennett by restricting full death benefit payments when death results from suicide within two years of policy issuance.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc" target="fb3c374d-3ef3-47c4-aa50-e800d1a94c74">
  <data key="d3">While the standard death benefit applies if the insured dies during the policy term with all premiums paid, it excludes coverage for suicides occurring within the first two years, reducing the payout to just the sum of premiums paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc" target="0f671b08-fa0b-4646-bec0-c87a883bbc17">
  <data key="d3">A suicide clause within two years limits the death benefit, potentially preventing the fulfillment of the promise to pay within 30 days unless the condition triggers a reduced refund instead of full coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc" target="1c9f056b-0c28-4ea8-968e-bcad5bdf0380">
  <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion applies even if death occurs during aircraft operation, unless specifically exempted—but since private flying is covered, the broader death-in-flight provision does not override the suicide clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc" target="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies that suicide within two years leads to no death benefit beyond premium repayment; fact_sentence_2 reinforces that after two years, the insurer cannot contest claims, making the suicide clause enforceable but non-disputable post-two-year threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
