  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8ea9b97-e6e5-4489-be08-3c5ea87c5638" target="2e5a669a-0eb1-4593-9d03-afb101531af9">
  <data key="d3">Rider 1 provides a premium waiver for those disabled, but requires yearly submission of proof of continued disability to maintain eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8ea9b97-e6e5-4489-be08-3c5ea87c5638" target="46cb3cb8-08d3-4e7b-b4bd-f8bf8ce53a84">
  <data key="d3">The $102 yearly premium for the Waiver of Premium due to Disability rider enables access to a benefit where future premiums are fully waived if the policyholder becomes disabled. This creates a direct link between paying the initial fee and receiving substantial relief later.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8ea9b97-e6e5-4489-be08-3c5ea87c5638" target="163ecb38-9f43-4a25-92c7-e5a3e53c0436">
  <data key="d3">The $102 yearly premium cited for Rider 1 corresponds precisely to the waiver-of-premium provision described under the same rider, reinforcing its intended use.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8ea9b97-e6e5-4489-be08-3c5ea87c5638" target="f4d7d65a-2757-4f6a-a581-628d6583aff0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes Rider 1 as a premium waiver for disability, consistent with chunk summary 1's explanation that it eliminates annual payments upon disability; fact_sentence_1 quantifies this by stating the premium amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
