<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="b8ea9b97-e6e5-4489-be08-3c5ea87c5638">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the insured become totally disabled before age 60 determines whether they qualify for the $102 annual premium on the Waiver of Premium rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables premium</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="46cb3cb8-08d3-4e7b-b4bd-f8bf8ce53a84">
  <data key="d3">If the insured becomes totally disabled before age 60, they qualify for Rider 1, triggering the automatic waiver of all future premiums under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional consequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="2bf72187-e922-4864-8481-8171333a1cb9">
  <data key="d3">If the insured becomes totally disabled before age 60, the premium waiver rider activates, ensuring ongoing coverage without further payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional continuation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f">
  <data key="d3">The first fact sets the prerequisite condition—that the insured must become totally disabled before age 60—for Rider 1 to apply. The second fact adds a necessary continuation: the disability must persist for six consecutive months to qualify for benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="b268c72e-1272-4e20-9941-6431b25ee80f">
  <data key="d3">If the insured becomes totally disabled before age 60, the premium waiver begins. It continues until recovery, return to work, or reaching age 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional effect</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="2e5a669a-0eb1-4593-9d03-afb101531af9">
  <data key="d3">If the insured qualifies for Rider 1 due to total disability before age 60, they must submit annual proof of continued disability to maintain coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 outlines qualification based on total disability prior to age 60, while fact sentence 2 specifies chronic illness requiring inability to perform multiple daily activities. Though different in condition type, both serve similar protective purposes by enabling payouts upon serious health decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="f4d7d65a-2757-4f6a-a581-628d6583aff0">
  <data key="d3">The $102 annual premium waiver under Rider 1 is conditional on total disability occurring before age 60, linking the financial relief directly to this eligibility threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="163ecb38-9f43-4a25-92c7-e5a3e53c0436">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines the nature of Rider 1—the premium waiver—but relies on fact_sentence_2 to define when it takes effect: specifically, if total disability occurs before age 60.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 1, applicable on total disability before age 60, contributes to the increased annual premium of $1,089 detailed in the primary fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
