<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="b8ea9b97-e6e5-4489-be08-3c5ea87c5638">
  <data key="d3">The 6-month continuous disability requirement ensures that only those who meet severe disability thresholds qualify for the premium waiver, making it essential for justifying the $102 yearly premium charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the disability last six consecutive months depends on the prior occurrence of total disability before age 60. Without meeting the initial onset condition, the duration threshold cannot be evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="46cb3cb8-08d3-4e7b-b4bd-f8bf8ce53a84">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of being disabled for six consecutive months triggers the automatic waiver of future premiums under Rider 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="2bf72187-e922-4864-8481-8171333a1cb9">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of six consecutive months of disability triggers the activation of the premium waiver, ensuring uninterrupted coverage thereafter.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional continuation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="2e5a669a-0eb1-4593-9d03-afb101531af9">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of being disabled for six consecutive months sets the foundation for eligibility under Rider 1. Annual proof of continuing disability ensures compliance with the policy’s terms beyond the initial waiting period.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="b268c72e-1272-4e20-9941-6431b25ee80f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of six consecutive months of disability triggers the premium waiver under Rider 1, which continues until the insured recovers, resumes work, or turns 65.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4">
  <data key="d3">The six-month disability requirement in Rider 1 likely relies on assessments of impaired daily functioning, such as difficulties in activities like bathing and dressing. These activities help determine if the disability threshold is met.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9">
  <data key="d3">Rider 1 sets a time-based criterion (six months of disability) for receiving benefits, whereas Rider 3 uses functional decline (inability to perform ADLs) as its basis. While not directly dependent, both serve similar purposes by enabling payouts under severe health deterioration.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="f4d7d65a-2757-4f6a-a581-628d6583aff0">
  <data key="d3">The six-month disability clause in Rider 1 directly enables the $102 premium waiver described in the earlier statement, making it conditional on sustained disability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="163ecb38-9f43-4a25-92c7-e5a3e53c0436">
  <data key="d3">The six-month disability requirement ensures that only individuals with prolonged incapacity qualify for premium waivers, supporting the rider’s intent to protect financially vulnerable policyholders.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for a 6-month disability duration (fact_sentence_2) explains part of why certain riders increase the total annual premium to $1,089 (fact_sentence_1), showing how rider conditions contribute to the final cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9e1fdeaf-67f1-42fa-966a-33413c85f595" target="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
</edge>
