<edge source="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13" target="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9">
  <data key="d3">The zero-cost nature of the rider ensures affordability, enabling beneficiaries to access substantial funds when needed most due to a terminal illness diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13" target="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 provides a terminal illness accelerated death benefit without charging extra premiums, but the actual payout is diminished over time due to an annual actuarial discount applied to account for early disbursement risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary term</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13" target="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 provides a terminal illness acceleration feature without extra premium costs. After a portion of the death benefit is paid out due to terminal illness, the remainder is still available for distribution to beneficiaries upon the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">no cost to use</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13" target="586acb2a-853b-4ebd-8a84-7e996761219c">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 provides terminal illness acceleration without extra cost, whereas Rider 3 offers chronic illness acceleration with a fixed annual fee. Both serve similar purposes but vary in terms of cost and condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">differs in cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 explains that the terminal illness rider is offered at no additional cost, which aligns with the inclusive pricing reflected in fact_sentence_1’s total annual premium of $1,089.</data>
  <data key="d4">no additional cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
