<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13">
  <data key="d3">Access to up to 95% of the death benefit during a terminal illness justifies the inclusion of the rider at no extra premium, enhancing its value proposition.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 permits early access to 95% of the death benefit upon terminal illness diagnosis, but the payout is diminished annually due to an actuarial discount applied to account for timing and risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="d0d2ce43-5e55-4cc3-9f0f-81e63f182a2b">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 enables early access to funds when a terminal illness is diagnosed, and the maximum allowable advance under this provision is capped at $500,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they may receive up to 95% of the death benefit through Rider 2, though the actual advance cannot be less than $10,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9">
  <data key="d3">When an individual is diagnosed with a terminal illness, they may receive up to 95% of the death benefit from Rider 2 while still alive. After the insured passes away, any unused portion of the original death benefit is distributed to designated beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 describes eligibility for a terminal illness acceleration benefit, whereas fact sentence 2 outlines requirements for a chronic illness-based payout. While both relate to advanced health impairments enabling early benefit access, they apply to distinct clinical scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 provides substantial pre-death payouts (up to 95%) for terminal illness, whereas Rider 3 caps advances at 50%, reflecting different risk thresholds and eligibility rules across similar but separate benefit categories.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2, described in fact_sentence_2 as providing early payout for terminal illness, contributes to the overall premium increase reflected in fact_sentence_1’s total annual cost of $1,089.</data>
  <data key="d4">contributes to cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
