<edge source="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96" target="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9">
  <data key="d3">A minimum advance of $10,000 ensures that even when accessing funds via Rider 2 due to a terminal illness, the beneficiary receives at least this amount, regardless of the total death benefit size.</data>
  <data key="d4">minimum threshold</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96" target="d0d2ce43-5e55-4cc3-9f0f-81e63f182a2b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 specifies the lowest amount that can be advanced under Rider 2, setting a baseline for eligibility. This provides context for understanding the full scale of potential payouts described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96" target="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0">
  <data key="d3">The minimum advance of $10,000 sets the baseline payout from Rider 2, but this amount is subject to reduction each year due to an 8% annual actuarial discount applied to the accelerated benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">sets baseline</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96" target="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 allows policyholders to receive a minimum advance of $10,000, which directly impacts the amount that remains payable to beneficiaries upon the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 offers a $10,000 minimum advance, which aligns with the expanded benefits described in the summary; these enhancements are reflected in the increased total premium of $1,089 compared to the base rate, showing how rider features influence pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
