  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0" target="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9">
  <data key="d3">An annual actuarial discount of roughly 8% reduces the accelerated death benefit paid out under Rider 2, meaning recipients receive less than the full 95% initially available upon terminal illness diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0" target="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96">
  <data key="d3">An 8% yearly actuarial discount reduces the accelerated death benefit under Rider 2, meaning any advance—such as the minimum $10,000—is progressively lowered over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces over time</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0" target="d0d2ce43-5e55-4cc3-9f0f-81e63f182a2b">
  <data key="d3">An annual actuarial discount of roughly 8% reduces the actual payout from the maximum advance of $500,000 under Rider 2, affecting the total accessible benefit over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0" target="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9">
  <data key="d3">The actuarial discount applied to the accelerated benefit reduces the total available payout, leaving a residual death benefit that becomes payable upon the insured's death.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0" target="9074adae-f9ba-4a37-87a1-710b818029e7">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2’s accelerated benefit includes an annual 8% actuarial discount, decreasing future payouts. In contrast, Rider 3 does not apply any actuarial discount to advance payments, preserving full value at disbursement.</data>
  <data key="d4">differs from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2’s declining accelerated benefit, discounted by 8% annually, contributes to the composition of the total annual premium of $1,089, reflecting how ongoing rider costs influence the final policy price.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
