<edge source="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9" target="5a454711-2bc0-411b-9675-9c153582bf13">
  <data key="d3">After the insured passes away, any unclaimed portion of the death benefit from Rider 2 remains payable to beneficiaries. This outcome depends on prior eligibility for the terminal illness benefit, which itself carries no added premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">payment outcome</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9" target="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9">
  <data key="d3">After the insured dies, the remaining balance of the death benefit under Rider 2 is paid out to beneficiaries. This occurs only after a prior withdrawal of up to 95% of the benefit was made while the insured was alive due to a terminal diagnosis.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9" target="c5bd960b-0752-414d-aad3-97a1a305bf96">
  <data key="d3">After any advance is made from Rider 2, such as the $10,000 minimum, the remainder of the death benefit continues to be paid to beneficiaries at the time of the insured's passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9" target="d0d2ce43-5e55-4cc3-9f0f-81e63f182a2b">
  <data key="d3">After an advance of up to $500,000 is made from Rider 2, the leftover portion of the death benefit remains payable to beneficiaries if the insured passes away before exhausting the full advance.</data>
  <data key="d4">remains after advance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9" target="fff349a0-c2b3-4147-8048-0595272170a0">
  <data key="d3">After the accelerated benefit is paid out with an annual 8% actuarial discount, the remainder of the death benefit is preserved and distributed to beneficiaries when the insured passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">residual of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1444f482-e5d8-4338-b319-a970f9d01ed9" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 2 contributes to the total annual premium of $1,089 by providing a death benefit payout to beneficiaries, which aligns with the broader protective intent described in the main policy summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
