  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="d037a900-e65d-46f1-97db-f750675f24fa">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">riders</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="a2bbbaf5-eb1b-4b1c-b8bd-f47818cd9768">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 describes eligibility tied to chronic illness impacting basic self-care functions, whereas fact sentence 1 covers pre-age-60 total disability. Both address significant health-related loss of function, though through differing clinical thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="f5a046c9-ad3b-4851-b4b9-55480dcafc4f">
  <data key="d3">Rider 3 focuses on loss of independence through impaired self-care abilities, contrasting with Rider 1’s focus on duration of disability. Despite differing evaluation methods, both aim to support individuals facing extended incapacitation.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that chronic illness qualifies for benefit access when two or more ADLs are impaired, contrasting with fact sentence 1’s focus on terminal illness diagnosis. Both serve similar purposes but operate under different medical triggers.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="586acb2a-853b-4ebd-8a84-7e996761219c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to qualify for the chronic illness rider — inability to perform two or more activities of daily living — determines whether the rider’s associated $48 annual premium is relevant to the individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Activities of Daily Living in fact_sentence_2 provides necessary context for determining whether the insured meets the chronic illness criteria outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="8939b21f-f68d-40db-89a6-72aed8a58ea7">
  <data key="d3">If the insured meets the chronic illness threshold defined by inability to perform two or more ADLs, they become eligible to receive payments under Rider 3.</data>
  <data key="d4">eligibility leads to payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5">
  <data key="d3">If the insured meets the chronic illness criteria outlined in fact sentence 1, they become eligible for a benefit that is capped at 50% of the policy’s face amount, as specified in fact sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb">
  <data key="d3">If the insured meets the criteria for chronic illness due to inability in two or more daily activities, a licensed healthcare provider must verify this state through formal certification.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires certification</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="9074adae-f9ba-4a37-87a1-710b818029e7">
  <data key="d3">The qualification for receiving benefits under Rider 3 requires chronic illness impairing two or more daily activities. This triggers access to advance payments, which are issued at face value without any actuarial discount being applied.</data>
  <data key="d4">condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 3’s chronic illness provision, detailed in fact_sentence_2, is one of the supplementary coverages contributing to the overall $1,089 annual premium stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
