  <data key="d3">The definition of Activities of Daily Living provides the standard by which continuous disability—required annually for Rider 1—is evaluated.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4" target="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 relies on the list of Activities of Daily Living from fact_sentence_2 to establish when chronic illness qualifies for Rider 3 benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4" target="8939b21f-f68d-40db-89a6-72aed8a58ea7">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Activities of Daily Living establishes the functional criteria used to assess eligibility for benefits under Rider 3, such as chronic illness acceleration. This context explains why monthly payouts are permitted when the insured meets specified ADL thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4" target="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Activities of Daily Living provides the standard by which a chronic illness's impact on daily functioning is assessed, supporting the need for professional certification under Rider 3.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Activities of Daily Living in fact_sentence_2 helps explain the eligibility requirements for the chronic illness accelerated death benefit rider referenced in chunk_summary_1, which contributes to the overall premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
