<edge source="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5" target="773ac2bf-c8ee-48e5-99a2-8dedd0ce52c9">
  <data key="d3">While Rider 3 limits advances to 50% of the face amount for chronic illness, Rider 2 offers higher access (up to 95%) for terminal illness, illustrating varying levels of financial support based on condition severity.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5" target="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9">
  <data key="d3">The maximum advance available under Rider 3 is limited to 50% of the face amount, but only applies when the insured satisfies the chronic illness condition described in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits payment</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5" target="8939b21f-f68d-40db-89a6-72aed8a58ea7">
  <data key="d3">The total advance under Rider 3 cannot exceed 50% of the face amount, which implies that even if monthly withdrawals occur at the 2% rate, the cumulative sum is capped accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5" target="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb">
  <data key="d3">Rider 3 allows up to 50% of the policy's face amount as an advance if a chronic illness is certified by a qualified medical professional.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5" target="9074adae-f9ba-4a37-87a1-710b818029e7">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes the upper limit for advances under Rider 3 at 50% of the policy’s face amount. This structural constraint interacts directly with the absence of any actuarial discount, meaning borrowers receive full access to that capped amount without reductions based on risk assessment.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 3’s provision allowing up to 50% of the $750,000 face amount aligns with the broader policy framework described in the first summary, where added riders increase the total annual premium to $1,089.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
