<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="586acb2a-853b-4ebd-8a84-7e996761219c">
  <data key="d3">To receive the chronic illness accelerated death benefit, a licensed healthcare practitioner must confirm the condition; once qualified, the policyholder pays an annual premium of $48 for this rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="25532b26-15cf-439e-81bb-d1a42ef63fe9">
  <data key="d3">The need for a certified diagnosis from a licensed healthcare practitioner arises specifically when the insured qualifies for chronic illness under the rider’s eligibility terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables validation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="f18fc48e-98d0-411b-90bf-83eff84b25c4">
  <data key="d3">Certification by a licensed healthcare practitioner confirms that the individual meets the medical criteria—such as inability to perform key ADLs—for receiving benefits under the chronic illness rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="8939b21f-f68d-40db-89a6-72aed8a58ea7">
  <data key="d3">To qualify for monthly payments under Rider 3, the insured’s chronic illness status must first be certified by a licensed healthcare practitioner.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="63574a8d-028b-4e11-96b6-a8a861f0e4a5">
  <data key="d3">To receive up to 50% of the face amount via Rider 3, a licensed healthcare provider must first confirm the insured meets chronic illness criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="59a0f1ea-2c5e-4e7f-b51c-fc1ba344210e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for medical certification under Rider 3 aligns with the general rule that adding riders necessitates proof of insurability, suggesting that documentation supporting chronic illness would be part of that evidence.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d5748a6-95ed-4858-bcb7-b5522f2bccfb" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Rider 3's requirement for physician certification on chronic illness status explains part of why additional premiums were added to the base rate; without this condition being met, the rider remains inactive despite contributing to the overall cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
