<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">The $750,000 accidental death benefit applies only when the accident is the immediate and sole cause of death, ensuring clarity on qualifying conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional requirement</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d3">The $750,000 accidental death benefit applies only when death follows an accident within 90 days; otherwise, the benefit does not activate despite the cause being accidental.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit applies only if death stems from an accident; however, it does not apply if the cause of death is suicide, thus narrowing the conditions under which the payout occurs.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit applies only when death stems from unintentional injury; self-inflicted injury is explicitly excluded, ensuring the benefit is reserved for true accidents rather than deliberate acts.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit applies only if death stems from an accident, but excludes cases involving war. War-related fatalities fall outside the covered scenarios despite meeting the general "accidental" criterion.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit applies broadly to injuries causing death but excludes cases where the insured died in an aviation incident while serving as pilot or crew. This limitation refines the conditions under which the primary benefit is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">If death occurs due to an accident, the $750,000 benefit applies unless the individual was intoxicated at the time of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit applies only if death occurs due to an accident; however, it does not apply if the individual was under the influence of drugs at the time of death, thus limiting the scope of eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit provides a fixed payout upon qualifying death; if such a death happens during the grace period, the insurer deducts any overdue premiums before disbursing the remaining balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">The $750,000 accidental death benefit is funded through the $94 yearly premium, establishing a direct financial linkage.</data>
  <data key="d4">funding source</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states the Death Benefit includes $750,000 for accidental injury-related deaths, which corresponds exactly to the condition outlined in fact_sentence_1 regarding Rider 5’s payout terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the trigger for the accidental death benefit ($750,000 payout upon death from accident), which supports and operationalizes the requirement in fact_sentence_1 that the accident must be the direct cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes the $750,000 accidental death benefit contingent on death occurring within 90 days of an accident, directly supporting the requirement outlined in fact_sentence_1 about timely claim submission.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The $1,089 annual premium encompasses costs associated with the $750,000 accidental death benefit rider, making it a component of the full policy pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of premium paid</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The accidental death benefit depends on the ongoing validity of the policy, meaning it ceases when the policy expires on July 12, 2054.</data>
