<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">For the $750,000 accidental death benefit to be triggered, the death must result directly from an accident, establishing a necessary condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables benefit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that the accident be the direct cause of death ensures only genuine accidents trigger the benefit, setting the stage for the subsequent time-bound condition where death must occur within 90 days.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the condition that death must be directly caused by an accident; fact_sentence_2 further restricts eligibility by explicitly excluding suicide, reinforcing the requirement for a non-intentional, external cause of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the condition that death must result directly from an accident, and fact_sentence_2 further excludes cases where the injury was self-inflicted, ensuring only truly external accidents trigger the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the core requirement that death must result directly from an accident, and fact_sentence_2 further refines this by explicitly excluding war-related incidents from consideration, ensuring clarity about non-covered scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring direct causation of death by an accident excludes aviation incidents where the insured was involved as pilot or crew, ensuring that certain high-risk scenarios do not trigger the benefit despite meeting the general causal condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the condition that death must be directly caused by an accident; fact_sentence_2 reinforces this by specifying that intoxication invalidates the claim, thus narrowing the scope of qualifying accidents.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">If an accident is not the direct cause of death, the benefit is denied; similarly, if the insured was intoxicated, the benefit is also voided regardless of causality.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="024f312c-2a82-4c4b-9492-447ba61bada0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death must be directly caused by an accident limits eligibility for the benefit, but this benefit ceases entirely once the insured turns 70, making the causal criterion irrelevant beyond that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="d617fcfa-ca1a-42af-b96a-3031b196a810">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that accidents must be the direct cause of death ensures claim validity, while RIDER 6 facilitates future increases in coverage capacity without health screening, supporting long-term protection planning.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="b8cb3948-8eb7-4978-b2b6-d2d8621a4b18">
  <data key="d3">The rule that death must be directly caused by an accident ensures claim validity for the death benefit, which could influence decisions to exercise the rider at age 49 to secure higher protection before potential health changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death must be directly due to an accident defines the scope of the $94-per-year accidental death benefit, ensuring its payout aligns with defined risk parameters.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that an accident must be the direct cause of death ensures that the $750,000 payout outlined in fact_sentence_1 applies only when the causal link between the accident and death is clear and unambiguous.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the universal criterion—accident must be the direct cause of death—for claiming the accidental death benefit, which specifically applies to Rider 5 as detailed in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">The direct causation rule reinforces the urgency of the 90-day window, ensuring claims are tied strictly to accidents without intervening causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 outlines a critical condition for accessing a portion of the policy's payout, which is referenced in fact_sentence_1 through the inclusion of riders and special benefits such as the accidental death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">For the accidental death benefit to be claimed, the incident must happen prior to the policy’s expiry on July 12, 2054, linking the condition of causality to the policy’s lifespan.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ee8ceda7-81eb-4537-9698-ad02c5b3ecf3" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is direct cause of</data>
</edge>
