<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">To receive the $750,000 accidental death benefit, death must happen within 90 days after the accident, making timing essential to triggering the payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">time restriction</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">For the death benefit to apply, not only must the accident be the direct cause, but the resulting death also needs to happen within 90 days, making timely occurrence dependent on prior causal linkage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur within 90 days of an accident sets a temporal condition for eligibility, which excludes certain types of incidents—like aviation accidents involving the insured—as defined in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets a temporal condition requiring death within 90 days of an accident, which complements fact_sentence_2’s exclusion of war-related incidents, ensuring that even timely deaths due to war do not trigger the benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">If death occurs within 90 days of an accident, the benefit may apply unless the deceased was intoxicated at the time, which nullifies the payout despite meeting the timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">The 90-day window for claiming the death benefit applies only if the death was not caused by intoxication; otherwise, even timely deaths are ineligible.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="024f312c-2a82-4c4b-9492-447ba61bada0">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur within 90 days of an accident applies universally but does not override the age-based termination of benefits at 70. Even if death occurs within 90 days, the payout is voided if the insured has reached age 70.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="d617fcfa-ca1a-42af-b96a-3031b196a810">
  <data key="d3">The 90-day requirement for accidental death benefits creates a time-sensitive context that may influence when the Guaranteed Insurability Rider should be exercised to secure future coverage before reaching certain milestones.</data>
  <data key="d4">temporal context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="177ee328-91d5-42c3-be6e-22a540d6f1cb">
  <data key="d3">Fact 1 specifies a deadline for claiming the accidental death benefit based on timing post-accident. Fact 2 describes a similar timeframe for utilizing a rider to increase coverage. Both rely on timely action but apply to different aspects of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">time dependent</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur within 90 days of an accident sets the condition for eligibility for the death benefit. If death happens during the grace period due to an accident, the unpaid premium is deducted from the benefit, meaning timely payment affects final payout even if the death qualifies.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">To receive the accidental death benefit, the death must occur within 90 days of the accident; this timeframe determines whether the $94 yearly premium leads to payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">The $750,000 payout requires death from an accident within 90 days, making the time window a key determinant of whether the benefit is triggered.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">The 90-day timeframe ensures that deaths not directly linked to the accident over time do not trigger the benefit, reinforcing the necessity of direct causation emphasized in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that death must occur within 90 days after an accident to receive the death benefit, which matches the timing rule described in fact_sentence_1 regarding Rider 5's payout terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that death occur within 90 days of an accident governs one component of the policy’s benefits, influencing why certain riders and premiums are included in the total annual cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The 90-day rule for accidental death claims depends on the policy being active; since it expires in 2054, any claim must also fall before that date to be eligible, making the expiration date a critical upper limit for claim viability.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="35bd29b2-6350-41b6-b843-ead50abe0aec" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies for death benefit if death occurs within 90 days of accident</data>
</edge>
