</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">Since suicide disqualifies a claim for the accidental death benefit, the payment is restricted to cases involving genuine accidents rather than self-inflicted causes.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 excludes suicide from the death benefit, fact_sentence_1 ensures that only accidents—excluding self-inflicted causes such as suicide—are considered valid triggers, thus maintaining consistency in defining eligible incidents.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 excludes suicide from eligibility for the death benefit. Fact sentence 2 extends that exclusion to include any self-inflicted injury, reinforcing the restriction on intentional acts against oneself.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that suicide is not covered under the accidental death benefit. This exclusion operates independently alongside other disqualifying circumstances such as war-related deaths, ensuring consistent application of policy limitations.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states suicide is not covered; similarly, fact sentence 2 excludes payouts when the insured was intoxicated. Both serve as distinct but related exclusionary criteria preventing claim settlement.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that suicide is not covered, while fact sentence 2 adds that intoxication also voids the benefit. Together, they expand on exclusionary conditions tied to intent and state of mind at death.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of suicide establishes one boundary condition for claiming the accidental death benefit, while the exclusion of aviation incidents involving the insured further narrows eligibility based on specific circumstances. Both serve similar purposes—limiting payout scope—but apply to different scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">While the accidental death benefit excludes suicide as a qualifying cause, its $94 yearly premium reflects the risk profile of covering non-suicidal accidental deaths, consistent with the broader rider's design.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">While the accidental death benefit covers injuries resulting in death, it does not apply if the death is due to suicide—a key exception highlighted in the second statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of suicide supports the necessity that the death be due solely to an external accident, reinforcing the causal link required by the accidental death benefit clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of suicide reinforces the timing condition by ensuring that only non-intentional, accident-related deaths within 90 days are covered, narrowing the pool of eligible claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The policy's exclusion of suicide affects eligibility for benefits, whereas the stated premium of $1,089 accounts for these very exclusions through its rate-setting mechanism based on underwriting class.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The suicide exclusion impacts potential claims before the policy expires, making it relevant to assess whether the beneficiary could receive funds even if the policy ends after July 12, 2054.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
