<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">Because self-inflicted injury disqualifies claims, it reinforces the requirement in the primary fact that the death must result from an actual accident, narrowing eligibility criteria.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury (fact_sentence_2) supports the requirement that the accident must be the direct cause of death (fact_sentence_1), preventing intentional acts from being classified as eligible accidents.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that injuries intentionally caused by the insured are ineligible. Fact sentence 1 narrows this further by explicitly stating suicide is also excluded, ensuring clarity around deliberate self-harm.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that self-inflicted injuries do not qualify for the death benefit. Fact sentence 2 adds another exclusion: war-related deaths also do not qualify. Both serve similar purposes by defining non-covered causes of death.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury reinforces that intentional harm does not qualify for benefits, aligning with the rule that drug intoxication also disqualifies claims, ensuring consistency in preventing abuse of the accidental death provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury strengthens the condition that death must result purely from external accidents; it complements the rule against payments when intoxicated, ensuring intent or substance use does not trigger benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury from the accidental death benefit explains why certain claims would be denied, even if the event occurred accidentally—this contextualizes the cost and limitations tied to the $94 premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains limitation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces the specificity of fact_sentence_1 by ruling out self-inflicted injury as a qualifying cause, clarifying that only truly unintentional accidents trigger the $750,000 payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury prevents claims under Rider 5 even if an accident occurred, meaning such incidents cannot satisfy the "direct cause" criterion outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">Excluding self-inflicted injury reinforces the need for deaths to result from genuine accidents within the 90-day window, supporting the temporal condition set in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury from the death benefit explains why certain risks are priced into the overall premium; without this restriction, premiums might differ significantly due to increased claim likelihood.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains premium</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of self-inflicted injury limits when the death benefit may be paid, which interacts with the policy’s long-term duration outlined by its 2054 expiration date.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
