<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">Aviation-related fatalities involving the insured as pilot or crew are explicitly barred from triggering the $750,000 accidental death benefit, even if otherwise caused by an accident.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">Since aviation-related fatalities are explicitly excluded, even if caused directly by an accident, the necessity of direct causation does not apply in such cases, narrowing the applicability of the primary qualification clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation accidents involving the insured as pilot or crew member narrows the scope of eligible accidents, reinforcing the need for any such incident to still meet the 90-day post-accident death criterion to trigger benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59">
  <data key="d3">Excluding aviation-related fatalities due to the insured’s role as pilot or crew complements the broader exclusion of suicide, reinforcing the policy's intent to limit benefits to truly unforeseen, non-intentional accidents outside high-risk categories.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">Excluding aviation accidents when the insured acts as pilot or crew complements the exclusion of war-related deaths by further restricting claims based on occupational or hazardous contexts, ensuring consistency in defining ineligible circumstances for the accidental death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation-related fatalities applies independently but complements the broader prohibition on payments when the insured was under the influence of drugs, ensuring that high-risk activities and impaired states do not trigger benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation-related accidents reinforces the broader restriction on benefits when death occurs under risky circumstances, such as being under the influence of alcohol—both scenarios represent deliberate risk-taking behaviors that undermine eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes similarly</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation accidents from the accidental death benefit reduces the pool of eligible claims, thereby influencing the actuarial basis behind the $94 yearly premium charged for the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">While fact_sentence_2 restricts eligibility for the $750,000 accidental death benefit by excluding aviation incidents, it confirms the existence and amount of that benefit under non-excluded circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">qualifies benefit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation accidents in fact_sentence_2 restricts the otherwise broad requirement in fact_sentence_1—that the accident must be the direct cause of death—by invalidating claims arising from such scenarios regardless of causality.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">Even though death occurring within 90 days qualifies under the initial condition, being involved in an aviation accident disqualifies the claim entirely, nullifying the temporal criterion.</data>
  <data key="d4">nullifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation accidents from the death benefit affects the risk profile underlying the $1,089 annual premium, suggesting the insurer accounts for this limitation when setting pricing.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of aviation accidents affects the scope of coverage during the policy’s lifetime, reinforcing why knowing the expiration date (July 12, 2054) matters for determining applicable claims windows.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d9d66b6-f05b-4f3f-982e-8a4cbf981f2b" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">excluded from death benefit when occurring in aviation</data>
</edge>
