<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies while under the influence of drugs, the $750,000 accidental death benefit is voided, meaning the primary condition for payout fails despite other qualifying factors.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 excludes claims when the insured was intoxicated, which supports the need for a clear causal link between accident and death emphasized in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d3">Even if death occurred within 90 days of an accident, the benefit is not paid if the individual was under the influence of drugs, making intoxication a critical override condition.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 notes that drug use disqualifies claims; likewise, fact sentence 1 specifies suicide also voids eligibility. These statements function together as complementary exclusions in the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2">
  <data key="d3">Drug-induced impairment invalidates claim eligibility just as self-inflicted injury does, maintaining coherence in the policy’s intent to exclude deliberate or reckless conduct leading to death.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion of drug-induced deaths (sentence 2) complements the exclusion of war-related fatalities (sentence 1), collectively narrowing the scope of what constitutes a qualifying accident for the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies a claim regardless of cause, including aviation accidents, thereby strengthening the restriction already imposed on such incidents involving pilots or crew members.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that no death benefit is paid if the insured was under the influence of drugs at the time of death. This condition aligns with and reinforces fact sentence 2, which excludes benefits when alcohol was involved, forming part of a broader prohibition against intoxication-related claims.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="878ac5c5-197f-4b9e-9430-2a1fd25c7ff0">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies while intoxicated, the accidental death benefit does not pay out, regardless of the $94 annual premium already paid for the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="5006f094-181a-470d-ac3b-c7b521d9de76">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a restriction on the accidental death benefit mentioned in fact_sentence_1, invalidating claims when drug use contributed to death, thereby limiting its applicability.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exclusion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="9b19b8c2-d328-414e-b271-76cab099ce37">
  <data key="d3">If the insured died due to an accident while under the influence of drugs, the death would not qualify for the accidental death benefit despite being directly caused by the accident, thus undermining the condition stated in fact 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="d85e868a-f03c-4843-904f-562570994fbd">
  <data key="d3">The drug intoxication clause reinforces the need for timely reporting and proof of cause-of-death, consistent with the 90-day window required for Rider 5 payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a no-pay provision when intoxicated limits the effectiveness of the $1,089 annual premium's intended protection, particularly in cases involving substance use.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The exclusion for deaths due to drug use limits the applicability of the death benefit, but since the policy itself ends in 2054, any such claim would need to occur before that date to be considered.</data>
  <data key="d4">time dependent condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6d5b8793-d5bd-4f2a-850f-94793083d7d7" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes death benefit payment</data>
</edge>
