<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies the claimant from receiving the $750,000 accidental death benefit, regardless of whether the death resulted from an accident.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="4351e296-ad01-4b03-8073-cffdc596ce2d">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies a claim even if an accident caused death, reinforcing the need for the accident to be the sole direct cause without contributing factors such as substance use.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies any claim—even one occurring within the allowed 90-day timeframe—rendering the timing condition irrelevant in such cases.</data>
  <data key="d4">precludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="8ea7b659-7380-42ed-b6f1-e4cffbb45c59">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies claims, just as suicide does; both clauses serve similar purposes—excluding self-inflicted or impaired-death scenarios from coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="8f0204f1-a4f1-4add-9ba8-59760c0094b2">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies claims involving impaired judgment, aligning with the broader principle that self-harm or deliberate actions invalidate accidental death eligibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="c9a479ac-a21d-4893-8d96-0ee391ee4cb0">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication disqualifies claims just as war does—both are explicit exclusions mentioned in the policy’s terms regarding accidental death benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="58b732d1-91fb-4e00-8dd8-6c20dca4bfb3">
  <data key="d3">Intoxication at the time of death disqualifies a claim similarly to how involvement in aviation roles does, as both situations involve heightened personal responsibility and potential recklessness, aligning them as comparable grounds for denial.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes similarly</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="aedfd2a5-0d7e-477f-952c-d53e51f6f0f2">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that no payout occurs if the insured was intoxicated by alcohol at death. This supports and complements fact sentence 1, which covers drug intoxication, together establishing a comprehensive restriction on substance-impaired deaths.</data>
  <data key="d4">excludes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">While the premium amount covers comprehensive protection, its benefits are contingent upon avoiding excluded causes like alcohol-related deaths, thus limiting payouts even when premiums have been maintained.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on condition</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2e9feb03-b57e-4d0b-913c-d96f91607819" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">If the insured dies after July 12, 2054, the policy no longer applies; however, even before expiry, the death benefit may be denied due to intoxication, regardless of the policy’s active status.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to coverage</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
