  <data key="d3">Age 40 serves as a specific eligibility date for exercising the rider’s benefit, allowing additional coverage without medical underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="44e0a4ac-db25-49f7-aa54-1d094f1c0708">
  <data key="d3">Age 40 serves as a defined option date enabling the exercise of RIDER 6, allowing up to $100,000 in increased coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="177ee328-91d5-42c3-be6e-22a540d6f1cb">
  <data key="d3">Age 40 serves as a designated option date under the rider, triggering eligibility to increase coverage. The insured must act promptly within 90 days after reaching this milestone to secure the added protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies one eligible age (40) for exercising RIDER 6, while fact sentence 2 adds another qualifying age (46), expanding the range of possible exercise opportunities under the rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="fd499eef-7e7e-4325-9622-d0c882722492">
  <data key="d3">Age 40 is one of the designated option dates for exercising RIDER 6; at that point, the premium for added coverage depends on the insured's age and health classification at the time of purchase.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="48571610-7269-4220-a825-c8f2945f622d">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 identifies age 40 as an option date for exercising RIDER 6. This complements fact_sentence_2, which specifies that age 43 is also an allowable option date for the same rider.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="b8cb3948-8eb7-4978-b2b6-d2d8621a4b18">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies age 40 as an option date for RIDER 6, while fact sentence 2 adds that age 49 is also included among the available option dates, expanding on the range of qualifying ages.</data>
  <data key="d4">additional to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies age 40 as a qualifying event for exercising the rider's purchase option. Fact sentence 2 adds that having a child through birth or adoption also qualifies. Together, they expand the range of eligible triggering events.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef">
  <data key="d3">The ability to exercise options under RIDER 6 starts at age 40, but those same options expire entirely once the insured turns 50, limiting the window for action.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes and terminates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Age 40 is listed as an eligible option date for RIDER 6, consistent with the policy’s provision allowing additional coverage through a rider included in the $1,089 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
