  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies one eligible age (46) for exercising the rider; fact sentence 2 adds another later date (49), extending the window for potential coverage increases under the same rider provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201" target="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies age 46 as one of the qualifying times to exercise the rider, while fact sentence 2 adds that family-related life events like childbirth also qualify. Together, they expand the range of circumstances enabling ridership activation.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201" target="177ee328-91d5-42c3-be6e-22a540d6f1cb">
  <data key="d3">Age 46 is designated as an option date under the rider, triggering the opportunity to increase coverage. This eligibility window requires action within 90 days to activate the additional coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201" target="fd499eef-7e7e-4325-9622-d0c882722492">
  <data key="d3">Age 46 is one of the designated times when the rider may be exercised, allowing the insured to increase coverage; however, the actual premium for such added coverage depends on the individual’s age and risk profile at that moment.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201" target="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef">
  <data key="d3">The availability of an option at age 46 under RIDER 6 is limited by the rule that all such options expire once the insured turns 50, creating a defined timeframe for action.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201" target="d35ea843-3cf7-4434-abd8-5317e92704d1">
  <data key="d3">The ability to exercise the rider at age 46 is permitted because the policy remains guaranteed renewable through age 95, ensuring continued eligibility for such riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201" target="f02ad15a-f220-4368-928b-f055e35cac36">
  <data key="d3">The mention of age 46 as an option date for the rider provides a timeline for increasing coverage, whereas the ability to convert parts of the policy offers long-term adaptability. These features operate independently within the policy’s flexible design.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
