<edge source="b8cb3948-8eb7-4978-b2b6-d2d8621a4b18" target="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 identifies age 49 as a qualifying date for exercising the rider's purchase option. Fact sentence 2 adds that the birth or adoption of a child also qualifies. Together, they expand the range of circumstances under which additional coverage may be acquired.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b8cb3948-8eb7-4978-b2b6-d2d8621a4b18" target="fd499eef-7e7e-4325-9622-d0c882722492">
  <data key="d3">Age 49 is a designated opportunity to purchase extra coverage through RIDER 6, and at that point, the premium depends on the insured's current age and health-based risk category.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
