<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="87951d9a-26b1-4d25-a8f2-239ec1d0ae52">
  <data key="d3">The availability of RIDER 6, which costs $89 per year, is triggered by major life events including the birth or adoption of a child.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="d617fcfa-ca1a-42af-b96a-3031b196a810">
  <data key="d3">A child’s birth serves as a qualifying event that activates the right to add coverage via the rider, which otherwise requires no medical underwriting.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="44e0a4ac-db25-49f7-aa54-1d094f1c0708">
  <data key="d3">The birth or adoption of a child serves as a qualifying event that enables the exercise of the rider’s option to add up to $100,000 in additional coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="5f90df18-58e5-4575-9e58-d2c545796976">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 lists parenthood-related milestones—birth or adoption—as eligibility criteria for the rider. Fact sentence 1 complements this by including age 40 as another such milestone, broadening the scope of when the rider may be exercised.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="48571610-7269-4220-a825-c8f2945f622d">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that the birth or adoption of a child qualifies as an option date for the rider. This condition operates independently yet equivalently to fact sentence 1, where attaining age 43 also enables additional coverage purchase.</data>
  <data key="d4">equivalent event</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="247febe6-9b75-43a5-b350-13e76dd99201">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 lists significant personal milestones—such as having or adopting a child—as trigger points for purchasing extra coverage, complementing fact sentence 1's mention of age-based options like turning 46.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="b8cb3948-8eb7-4978-b2b6-d2d8621a4b18">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 specifies that the birth or adoption of a child activates the rider’s option to buy more coverage. Fact sentence 1 complements this by listing age 49 as another such trigger, showing multiple pathways to exercise the same right.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="177ee328-91d5-42c3-be6e-22a540d6f1cb">
  <data key="d3">Birth or adoption of a child activates the rider’s option to increase coverage; however, the insured must use this opportunity within 90 days after such an event.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef">
  <data key="d3">The ability to purchase additional coverage due to life events like childbirth is contingent upon being under age 50, after which all such options cease.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="92f0d544-ff95-4002-8c1e-cce1e2ed72b1">
  <data key="d3">The occurrence of a qualifying event such as childbirth enables the purchase of additional coverage via the rider, which contributes to the total premium amount stated in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="fd499eef-7e7e-4325-9622-d0c882722492">
  <data key="d3">The birth or adoption of a child triggers the right to increase coverage through RIDER 6, and the resulting premium for such added coverage is set according to the insured's age and health status at the time of exercise.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers pricing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The mention of child-related event dates for a rider aligns with the comprehensive nature of the policy’s premium, which accounts for potential future increases due to such qualifying events.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c4cc2e2-e0dd-43cc-9162-2c30fb8592d7" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">While Option Dates for Rider 6 allow enrollment based on major life events like having a child, these opportunities cease once the policy reaches its final expiration on July 12, 2054, making timing critical for utilization.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
