  <data key="d3">Once the insured turns 50, any prior eligibility based on events like childbirth becomes irrelevant because the rider’s options are terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">terminated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef" target="177ee328-91d5-42c3-be6e-22a540d6f1cb">
  <data key="d3">The termination of the rider at age 50 nullifies any future ability to use the 90-day window for buying additional coverage, effectively limiting the practical application of the timing rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">terminates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef" target="fd499eef-7e7e-4325-9622-d0c882722492">
  <data key="d3">RIDER 6 stops allowing new coverage purchases after age 50, meaning the conditions described in fact_sentence_1—such as age-based premium determination—are no longer applicable beyond that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on age limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">RIDER 6's termination at age 50 impacts the longevity of additional coverage options, though it does not affect the currently reported premium of $1,089.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9f917507-b0ee-48c4-98b8-f7fc168084ef" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">While Rider 6 terminates at age 50, the underlying policy continues until 2054, ensuring basic coverage persists even after rider benefits lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">complies with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
