  <data key="d3">Premiums are due annually, reflecting the fixed yearly cost of $94 for the base policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">amount basis</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="87951d9a-26b1-4d25-a8f2-239ec1d0ae52">
  <data key="d3">The annual payment mode applies to the rider’s premium, ensuring the $89 charge is due each year as part of the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to rider</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="92f0d544-ff95-4002-8c1e-cce1e2ed72b1">
  <data key="d3">The annual payment mode necessitates a fixed yearly cost, which is precisely $1,089.00 for the full policy including all riders.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="ff41a674-10ac-4c9e-a832-459e288b75df">
  <data key="d3">The annual payment mode explains why the premium has a fixed due date each year, such as July 12, as stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="03f96a62-9cac-4ba6-9b09-3d1ac7656341">
  <data key="d3">While the primary payment mode is annual, the policy permits switching to monthly payments when requested, offering financial flexibility without altering core terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04">
  <data key="d3">Since the premium is paid annually, the 31-day grace period serves as a buffer allowing continued coverage even if payment is delayed beyond the due date.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="9f62f637-e863-44b4-96e3-ef56704f581c">
  <data key="d3">The policy offers annual payment as the default option, but individuals may choose quarterly installments instead by requesting it. This provides financial flexibility for policyholders who prefer smaller, more frequent payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="e6de81af-aa16-485d-9cca-a6d0499ae0d5">
  <data key="d3">Since the premium is paid annually, it triggers a defined window—specifically a 31-day grace period—during which coverage stays active even if payment is delayed. This ensures continuity of benefits despite late payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for annual payment creates the context under which the grace period operates, making it possible for an unpaid premium to be deducted from the death benefit if death happens during that window.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="1c39a3e5-e052-494d-ba68-54005783ca3f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 specifies that premiums are due annually, setting the timing framework. Fact sentence 2 indicates that future renewal premiums may rise per a defined schedule, which applies within that same annual cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 indicates the premium is paid annually, which contextualizes the figure stated in fact_sentence_1, ensuring clarity on when and how often the $1,089 is required.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">Annual payment requirements ensure the policy remains active until it expires on July 12, 2054.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
