  <data key="d3">A monthly payment option is available upon request, allowing policyholders to spread out the annual premium of $94 into smaller installments.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03f96a62-9cac-4ba6-9b09-3d1ac7656341" target="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157">
  <data key="d3">Although monthly payments are possible on request, the default and stated method is annual payment, maintaining consistency with the original agreement.</data>
  <data key="d4">alternative to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03f96a62-9cac-4ba6-9b09-3d1ac7656341" target="9f62f637-e863-44b4-96e3-ef56704f581c">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that monthly payments are an option if requested. Fact sentence 2 indicates that quarterly payments are also available on request, representing another flexible payment choice unrelated to the first.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="03f96a62-9cac-4ba6-9b09-3d1ac7656341" target="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04">
  <data key="d3">The option for monthly payments provides flexible billing timing, which complements the 31-day grace period that maintains coverage beyond the due date. Together, they support ongoing premium affordability and continuity.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
