<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="ff41a674-10ac-4c9e-a832-459e288b75df">
  <data key="d3">After the July 12 due date, a 31-day grace period maintains coverage, allowing time to pay the annual premium without losing benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period depends on the annual payment cycle, ensuring temporary protection after the yearly deadline passes.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="03f96a62-9cac-4ba6-9b09-3d1ac7656341">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period ensures continued coverage even if a payment is late, making the availability of monthly payment modes more practical for maintaining consistent compliance without immediate lapse risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="e6de81af-aa16-485d-9cca-a6d0499ae0d5">
  <data key="d3">The 31-day grace period begins after the payment deadline, ensuring continuous protection without interruption.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="9f62f637-e863-44b4-96e3-ef56704f581c">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period accommodates delays in payment, making it relevant whether the policyholder chooses annual or quarterly billing modes. This supports the practicality of offering multiple payment frequencies.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e">
  <data key="d3">The grace period ensures ongoing coverage beyond the due date, allowing the insurer to pay claims even when premiums are late. In such cases, the unpaid amount is subtracted from the final death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period explains how the policy maintains validity despite potential delays in paying the $1,089 annual premium, ensuring uninterrupted protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">suppresses risk of lapse</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period means the policyholder has additional time to pay premiums without losing coverage, but the ultimate end-of-protection timeline still hinges on the fixed expiration date of July 12, 2054.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
