<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="5043b1c0-84fc-433c-a7be-9218b8545f5d">
  <data key="d3">If a claim arises during the grace period due to non-payment, the outstanding premium (such as the $94 base amount) is subtracted from the payout, meaning the actual benefit received could be reduced accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="80f0a3df-332f-4526-af6f-c0a508f1d61f">
  <data key="d3">When a claim arises during the grace period, the full death benefit is reduced by the outstanding premium, meaning the actual payout depends on whether the initial benefit was triggered under the policy’s terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="b938585a-fc9e-4358-bb77-95bbcf1e1f31">
  <data key="d3">Even if death occurs during the grace period and thus triggers a deduction for the unpaid premium, the death still needs to have occurred within 90 days of the accident to qualify for any benefit at all.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="92f0d544-ff95-4002-8c1e-cce1e2ed72b1">
  <data key="d3">If the death benefit is reduced by the unpaid premium during the grace period, it implies that the original premium was set at $1,089, establishing the baseline cost of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="ff41a674-10ac-4c9e-a832-459e288b75df">
  <data key="d3">If death happens during the 31-day grace period after missing the July 12 payment deadline, the unpaid premium is deducted from the payout, meaning timely payment by July 12 avoids such deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="219bffde-d1a5-460e-82a7-164eb4b6a157">
  <data key="d3">If death occurs during the grace period, the unpaid annual premium is subtracted from the payout, implying that the original annual payment obligation—stated in fact_sentence_1—is essential to determining the final benefit amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="5056bd4e-5477-4eaf-bb15-46b84bab7d04">
  <data key="d3">Death occurring during the grace period qualifies for the death benefit, contingent upon deduction of the overdue premium, which depends on the prior establishment of the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="e6de81af-aa16-485d-9cca-a6d0499ae0d5">
  <data key="d3">Since the death benefit is reduced by the unpaid premium when death happens during the grace period, it confirms that coverage was still effective throughout that interval.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="c37a8c56-c455-4223-bf63-099ad8e97416">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a grace period mentioned in fact_sentence_2 introduces a scenario where the full premium may not have been paid, thereby impacting the effective cost referenced in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9c3e6312-c3f4-4a65-ae25-1fdcea64f33e" target="4b0941c4-2ba4-47c4-820c-1ebace0a9c2c">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a 31-day grace period implies that even if the policyholder dies shortly after the July 12, 2054 renewal date, the policy remains effective temporarily, meaning the expiration date defines when the grace period begins and ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
