<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="b3e12914-fba7-442d-8f31-2161867e424e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without evidence of insurability depends on the policy being guaranteed renewable, which provides the foundation for future conversion options.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="6fc66133-3b01-4f07-88d6-90152fe6617b">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert without proof of insurability ensures accessibility, while the allowance before policy expiry defines the timeframe during which this option remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="6f9d5bb4-e0cd-4a27-94a4-c6105a8fa692">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert without proof of insurability ensures accessibility, while the requirement to act before age 70 sets a clear temporal boundary for exercising this option.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert without proof of insurability is limited by the earliest of age 70 or policy termination, ensuring the option remains viable only within a defined timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="0e09a261-66b0-4858-bea2-dde1aae36c41">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert without proof of insurability enables policyholders to transition coverage easily, but only if at least $50,000 worth of coverage is converted, ensuring a meaningful transfer while maintaining risk control.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="520ea8d4-9ede-4e65-88be-2ee9ab6039aa">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert without proof of insurability enhances policyholder benefits, while the narrow incontestability exception ensures insurers can only challenge claims over unpaid premiums, maintaining fairness.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="e225c316-9494-4db7-a2fa-eeff59066bd6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to change beneficiaries at any time complements the policy's overall flexibility, including conversion options, enhancing control over estate planning aspects.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="59a0f1ea-2c5e-4e7f-b51c-fc1ba344210e">
  <data key="d3">The first fact describes a lenient condition allowing conversion to permanent insurance without health verification, which contrasts with the second fact stating that adding riders generally requires evidence of insurability, suggesting inconsistent underwriting standards across policy adjustments.</data>
  <data key="d4">contrasts with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="d35ea843-3cf7-4434-abd8-5317e92704d1">
  <data key="d3">The ability to convert to permanent insurance without medical evidence enhances the utility of the lifelong renewability feature, allowing flexible transitions based on changing needs.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e" target="f02ad15a-f220-4368-928b-f055e35cac36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 confirms that conversion to permanent insurance is possible without proving insurability, supporting the feasibility of partial or full conversions mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
