  <data key="d4">section</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="b3e12914-fba7-442d-8f31-2161867e424e">
  <data key="d3">The rule limiting conversion to before age 70 or policy expiry implies that even if the policy renews beyond age 70, conversion rights cease at that milestone, thus constraining the scope defined by the lifelong renewability clause.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="ac3feceb-a7e7-49d3-b0d9-b4f248709b5e">
  <data key="d3">The deadline for conversion at age 70 or upon policy expiry enables the flexibility of converting without evidence of insurability up to that point.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="6fc66133-3b01-4f07-88d6-90152fe6617b">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes the maximum allowable time for conversion, thereby defining the temporal boundary within which the possibility mentioned in fact_sentence_1 applies.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="6f9d5bb4-e0cd-4a27-94a4-c6105a8fa692">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 defines the ultimate cutoff for conversion using both the insured’s age and the policy term; fact_sentence_1 reflects one component of this rule—that conversion must happen before age 70—thus serving as a subset of the full temporal restriction outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="0e09a261-66b0-4858-bea2-dde1aae36c41">
  <data key="d3">The maximum time window for converting coverage ends at age 70 or upon policy expiry, while any conversion must involve at least $50,000 in coverage. These constraints operate independently but jointly shape the conversion terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions conversion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="d35ea843-3cf7-4434-abd8-5317e92704d1">
  <data key="d3">Although the policy remains renewable until age 95, its conversion privilege terminates at age 70, meaning the lifetime renewability does not extend the deadline for converting to permanent insurance.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456" target="f02ad15a-f220-4368-928b-f055e35cac36">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 imposes a time limit on the conversion option referenced in fact_sentence_1, ensuring it can only be exercised under specific conditions tied to age or policy duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits conversion</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1ad687bb-ada5-4a9c-abe7-7e3c9df47fb5" target="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">determines conversion deadline through expiration date</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6a0e0d5a-ee88-4ef0-87a1-411e9ba2a821" target="a3c240d7-a2bf-45a9-8d80-9ad84d392456">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">limits conversion deadline</data>
</edge>
