<edge source="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3" target="b3e12914-fba7-442d-8f31-2161867e424e">
  <data key="d3">After two years of continuous coverage, the insurer cannot challenge claims, reinforcing confidence in the long-term viability of the policy, including its guaranteed renewal through age 95.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3" target="520ea8d4-9ede-4e65-88be-2ee9ab6039aa">
  <data key="d3">After two years of continuous coverage, the insurer cannot contest claims under the policy, but this protection does not apply if premiums have not been paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">exception to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3" target="d2c5d0f2-fe5f-40d2-938f-ede16175763c">
  <data key="d3">The insurer's inability to contest claims after two years ensures that beneficiaries receive payouts when eligible, including cases involving flight-related deaths. This supports the provision that passengers in aircraft are covered under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional covered</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3" target="b80cc6fe-51ef-4abd-83ab-c60076297fbc">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes that after two years, insurers lose the power to contest claims, which directly supports the validity and binding nature of the provision in fact_sentence_1 regarding suicide-related payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3" target="d35ea843-3cf7-4434-abd8-5317e92704d1">
  <data key="d3">The two-year non-contest rule strengthens confidence in the lifelong renewability provision, as it ensures that even decades-long policies won’t face retroactive challenges once past the initial probationary period.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3" target="f02ad15a-f220-4368-928b-f055e35cac36">
  <data key="d3">The non-contest provision strengthens confidence in the policy’s longevity, making the conversion option more valuable over time, especially when considering potential future needs beyond temporary term protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="06c89ceb-2d54-4813-94c6-73ad6660044c" target="c98a305d-6028-47a0-875f-d569080ab9a3">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">becomes incontestable after</data>
</edge>
